journal.threat.low=Low
journal.threat.medium=Medium
journal.threat.high=High
journal.blue_mercy_gourd.title=Blue Mercy Gourd
journal.blue_mercy_gourd.body=A rare early-zone fruit with cleansing pulp. It neutralizes poison traces and weak scent marks, but should not be treated as normal food.
journal.blue_mercy_gourd.advice=Use after contact with toxins or marking parasites. Do not waste it at full safety.
journal.ash_milk_fern.title=Ash Milk Fern
journal.ash_milk_fern.body=Grey fern with thick sealing sap. The sap closes shallow wounds and stabilizes small cuts.
journal.ash_milk_fern.advice=Good for minor damage. Avoid relying on it for deep, dirty wounds.
journal.halo_tear_succulent.title=Halo Tear Succulent
journal.halo_tear_succulent.body=Morning drops clean biological slime from skin, tools and visor surfaces. Older drops become harsher.
journal.halo_tear_succulent.advice=Use it to remove traces before night movement.
journal.pulsefruit_column.title=Pulsefruit Column
journal.pulsefruit_column.body=A pulsing succulent that stores water, salts and sugars. The resource is useful, but the plant can punish greedy harvesting.
journal.pulsefruit_column.advice=Drink when exhausted or drowsy. Leave before cutting too deep.
journal.blood_lantern_fig.title=Blood Lantern Fig
journal.blood_lantern_fig.body=High-energy fruit with a warm red glow. It restores strength, but makes the body smell obvious to night hunters.
journal.blood_lantern_fig.advice=Use only when health matters more than stealth.
journal.funnel_tongue_grazer.title=Funnel Tongue Grazer
journal.funnel_tongue_grazer.body=A calm grazer that cleans parasites and slime from larger bodies. Its help is useful, but rough.
journal.funnel_tongue_grazer.advice=Follow cleaning traces to remove marks, but keep wounds covered.
journal.mossback_grazer.title=Mossback Grazer
journal.mossback_grazer.body=A peaceful herd animal carrying smaller life on its back. It is not hunting you, but herd panic can kill.
journal.mossback_grazer.advice=Circle herds from the front and side at distance. Never cross through them.
journal.lantern_mite.title=Lantern Mite
journal.lantern_mite.body=A small glowing parasite that makes warm bodies visible at night and attracts predators.
journal.lantern_mite.advice=Remove the glow before moving through dark open ground.
journal.needle_skipper.title=Needle Skipper
journal.needle_skipper.body=A small jumper that punctures soft plant tissue and may mistake resting bodies or gear for food.
journal.needle_skipper.advice=Shake boots and packs. Do not sleep on open soft ground.
journal.drift_tortoise.title=Drift Tortoise
journal.drift_tortoise.body=A slow shell-bearer with sheltered pockets. Other creatures may use it as cover during rain.
journal.drift_tortoise.advice=Useful as temporary shelter, but check what already hides there.
journal.rain_choir_frog.title=Rain Choir Frog
journal.rain_choir_frog.body=A soft frog that sings before pressure changes. Its choir warns that the ecosystem is about to switch mode.
journal.rain_choir_frog.advice=When they sing, prepare for rain and moving parasites.
journal.velvet_snapjaw.title=Velvet Snapjaw
journal.velvet_snapjaw.body=A silent predator sign near the night edge. It hunts weakened or distracted prey from cover.
journal.velvet_snapjaw.advice=Avoid bushes and darkness while marked or injured.
journal.capsule_wake_point.title=Capsule wake point
journal.capsule_wake_point.body=Initial crash shelter. The capsule feels safe, but it cannot remain isolated from the living world.
journal.capsule_wake_point.advice=Use it as orientation, not as a permanent home.
journal.first_herd_reading_scene.title=First herd reading
journal.first_herd_reading_scene.body=The herd is not a single creature. It is a moving ecosystem of grazers, mites, plants and hunters.
journal.first_herd_reading_scene.advice=Read what follows the herd before approaching it.
journal.frond_visibility_gate.title=Frond visibility gate
journal.frond_visibility_gate.body=Ribbon growth makes simple paths harder to read and gives small life a place to hide.
journal.frond_visibility_gate.advice=Slow down before entering dense fronds.
journal.wet_lobe_false_safety.title=Wet lobe false safety
journal.wet_lobe_false_safety.body=Wet ground looks soft and protective, but gathers parasites, spores and unstable soil.
journal.wet_lobe_false_safety.advice=Do not rest in wet hollows.
journal.ridge_first_overlook.title=Ridge overlook
journal.ridge_first_overlook.body=Higher ground gives route knowledge. It also exposes movement to watchers.
journal.ridge_first_overlook.advice=Use ridges to plan, then move before night.
journal.tortoise_rain_shelter_scene.title=Tortoise shelter sign
journal.tortoise_rain_shelter_scene.body=A shell can become temporary weather cover. It is also a shared refuge for smaller organisms.
journal.tortoise_rain_shelter_scene.advice=Check the shelter before entering it.
journal.night_demasking_field.title=Night demasking field
journal.night_demasking_field.body=At night, light, scent and pollen matter more than silhouettes. A marked body becomes a signal.
journal.night_demasking_field.advice=Clean markings before crossing this field.
journal.lowland_transition_warning.title=Lowland transition warning
journal.lowland_transition_warning.body=The next route drops toward wetter soil, more parasites and less stable ground.
journal.lowland_transition_warning.advice=Enter prepared: clean, healed and with resources saved.

